{"path":"numeric/valarray/abs","title":"std::abs(std::valarray)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>abs<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(std::valarray)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/abs","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes absolute value of each element in the value array.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/valarray\">&lt;valarray&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> abs<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> va <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes absolute value of each element in the value array.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> va\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> value array to apply the operation to\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Value array containing absolute values of the values in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">va</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Unqualified function (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">abs</span></code>) is used to perform the computation. If such function is not available, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">abs</span></span></code> is used due to <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a>.\n</p><p>The function can be implemented with the return type different from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span>. In this case, the replacement type has the following properties:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> All <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span> member functions of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span> are provided.\n</li><li> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/slice_array\">std::slice_array</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/gslice_array\">std::gslice_array</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/mask_array\">std::mask_array</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/indirect_array\">std::indirect_array</a></span> can be constructed from the replacement type.\n</li><li> For every function taking a <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx11\"><span>except <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/begin2\"><code>begin()</code></a> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/end2\"><code>end()</code></a></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></span></span>, identical functions taking the replacement types shall be added;\n</li><li> For every function taking two <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> arguments, identical functions taking every combination of <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> and replacement types shall be added.\n</li><li> The return type does not add more than two levels of template nesting over the most deeply-nested argument type.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<table class=\"eq-fun-cpp-table\">\n<tr>\n<td>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\nvalarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> abs<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> va<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> other <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> va<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> i <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> other<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> abs<span class=\"br0\">(</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> other<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// proxy object may be returned</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;valarray&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> v<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">4</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">5</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">6</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">7</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">8</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> v2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">abs</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> n <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> v2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/abs\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>abs<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(int)</span></span><span>labs</span><span>llabs</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes absolute value of an integral value (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small{|x|}\">|x|</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/fabs\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>abs<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(float)</span></span><span>fabs</span><span>fabsf</span><span>fabsl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  absolute value of a floating point value (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small{|x|}\">|x|</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/abs\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>abs<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the magnitude of a complex number <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/valarray","title":"std::valarray"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::abs(std::valarray)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Computes absolute value of each element in the value array."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"va"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Value array containing absolute values of the values in va."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Unqualified function (abs) is used to perform the computation. If such function is not available, std::abs is used due to argument-dependent lookup."},{"label":"Possible implementation"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"abs(int), labs, llabs","note":"computes absolute value of an integral value (|x|)"},{"label":"abs(float), fabs, fabsf, …","note":"absolute value of a floating point value (|x|)"},{"label":"abs(std::complex)","note":"returns the magnitude of a complex number"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":280,"codeBlockCount":3}
